.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt MICROINIT.JSON 5
.Os "BigFred OS"
.Sh NAME
.Nm microinit.json
.Nd service configuration for microinit
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /data/etc/microinit.json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
JSON configuration loaded by
.Xr microinit 8
after early-boot.
Created automatically if missing
.Pq empty services list
together with
.Pa microinit.json.example .
.Ss Top-level fields
.Bl -tag -width restartBackoff
.It Cm version
Config schema version (currently 1)
.It Cm logs.tty
TTY for mixed service logs (default
.Pa /dev/tty2 )
.It Cm logs.initTty
TTY for microinit operational logs (default
.Pa /dev/tty3 )
.It Cm logs.lines
Ring-buffer capacity in memory (default 300)
.It Cm logs.logToFiles
If true, append lines to per-service files under
.Cm logs.dir
.Pq default false ;
also enabled by
.Nm microinit Cm init Fl -log-to-files
.Pq keeps RAM + TTY only on read-only / embedded roots when false
.It Cm logs.dir
Directory for per-service
.Pa .log
files when
.Cm logs.logToFiles
is true (default
.Pa /data/logs )
.It Cm socket
Unix control socket path
.It Cm console
Console TTY for status and getty
.It Cm openTelemetry.enable
If true and the binary includes OpenTelemetry
.Pq default build; omit with
.Cm cargo build Fl -no-default-features
.Pc ,
export OTLP metrics to
.Cm openTelemetry.endpoint
.Pq Grafana Alloy OTLP/HTTP default
.Pa http://127.0.0.1:4318
.It Cm openTelemetry.endpoint , protocol , serviceName , exportIntervalSecs , headers
OTLP client parameters
.Pq protocol http only in the current build
.It Cm services
Array of service objects
.El
.Ss Drop-in directories
After loading this file,
.Nm
merges
.Pa $DATA_DIR/etc/microinit.d/services/**/*.json
in lexicographic path order
.Pq later wins for the same service name ,
then applies
.Xr microinit.services.enabled-override.json 5 .
Changes to these JSON files are picked up via Linux inotify
.Pq hot-reload without restarting microinit ;
.Cm socket
and
.Cm logs.*
changes require a process restart.
.Ss Service fields
.Bl -tag -width successExitCodes
.It Cm name
Unique identifier
.It Cm enabled
If false, skipped at boot; start/restart refused (default true)
.It Cm daemon
Long-lived process if true; one-shot job if false
.It Cm restart
Restart on crash when daemon (default false)
.It Cm restartBackoff
Seconds between restarts (default 2)
.It Cm successExitCodes
Exit codes treated as success (default
.Bq 0 )
.It Cm startWaitSecs
For
.Cm daemon
services: seconds to wait after start before deciding
.Dq Running
vs
.Dq Failed
.Pq default 0 .
If the process exits during this window, start is treated as failed
.Pq even with a success exit code .
When 0, a short SysV daemonize grace applies and a success exit is treated as
.Dq Running
.Pq forked daemon script .
.It Cm shutdownWaitSecs
Seconds to wait after stop signal / stopCmd before sending
.Dv SIGKILL
.Pq default 5
.It Cm background
Start in parallel; does not block boot (default false)
.It Cm dependsOn
Services that must be
.Cm Running
or
.Cm Succeeded
before start. Until then the service stays in
.Cm waiting_for_dependency
and starts automatically when ready; a manual
.Cm stop
cancels the wait.
.It Cm cmd
Base command; used as
.Dq cmd start|stop|restart
when specific cmds are null
.It Cm startCmd , stopCmd , restartCmd
Explicit shell commands
.It Cm env , cwd
Environment and working directory
.It Cm livenessProbe
Optional object. Exactly one of
.Cm cmd ,
.Cm httpUrl ,
or
.Cm tcpAddr
must be set.
Shared fields:
.Cm interval
in seconds
.Pq default 60
and
.Cm timeout
in seconds
.Pq default 5 .
.Cm cmd
uses
.Cm successExitCodes
.Pq default Bq 0 .
.Cm httpUrl
uses
.Cm httpMethod
.Pq default GET
and
.Cm httpAcceptedCodes
.Pq default Bq 200 .
.Cm tcpAddr
is
.Dq host:port
and succeeds if the TCP connect works.
While the service is
.Cm running ,
.Cm succeeded ,
or
.Cm failed ,
microinit probes every
.Cm interval
seconds; failure re-runs start.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
See
.Pa /data/etc/microinit.json.example
written on first boot.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr microinit 8 ,
.Xr microinit.services.enabled-override.json 5
